  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening and Decentralizing the National Response Against HIV in the Republic of Guinea - Guinea (01-Oct-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Guinea, HIV, Population Services International (PSI HQ)This program has the following goals: Reduce mortality and morbility for PLwHIV by at least 50% from 2013 to 2017.  Reduce new infections by 50% from 2013 to 2017. The objectives of this program are: From 2013 to 2017, at least 60% of key populations (MSM and PS) adopt a lower risk facing behavior STI / HIV.  From 2013 to 2017, at least 60% of young teens adopt a lower risk facing behavior STI / HIV.  From 2013 to 2017, at least 90% of children and adults living with HIV survive 12 months after initiation of ARV treatment.  From 2013 to 2017, the proportion of HIV transmission is reduced by 90% among children born to HIV positive mothers</narrative>
  </description>
